From: Chad Monroe <chad@monroe.io>
Date: Tue, 06 Oct 2026 18:58:13 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: mac80211: do not assign an AP_VLAN chanctx in the driver

An AP_VLAN shares the channel context of its AP and is never added to
the driver. A hardware restart still passed the AP_VLAN context to the
driver, which failed the in-driver check and logged a warning.

Signed-off-by: Chad Monroe <chad@monroe.io>
---
 net/mac80211/util.c |    4 ++++
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+)

--- a/net/mac80211/util.c
+++ b/net/mac80211/util.c
@@ -1718,6 +1718,10 @@ static void ieee80211_assign_chanctx(str
 
 	lockdep_assert_wiphy(local->hw.wiphy);
 
+	/* the driver does not know AP_VLANs; they share the AP's context */
+	if (sdata->vif.type == NL80211_IFTYPE_AP_VLAN)
+		return;
+
 	conf = rcu_dereference_protected(link->conf->chanctx_conf,
 					 lockdep_is_held(&local->hw.wiphy->mtx));
 	if (conf) {
